Brighter Pocket Companion sets up Brighter Shores only: no list of games.

Tolkara Management sets up any number of games from profiles, built in or added by the user;
Brighter Pocket carries one game (Joe, 2026-11-13: "everything should be specific to Brighter
Shores, so remove that layer of complexity"). The companion now reads only the source's
profiles/brighter-shores/profile.json and holds it as the model's one game:
- The Game step is the Brighter Shores step: no checkbox list, Games header, Add a Profile
  (from a file or a link), imported profiles or command-line footer; it shows the game
  straight away (Install in Steam, Open Steam, found on this Mac with Choose Another Folder
  and Show in Finder, or not found). A profile that cannot be read is one error.
- No account-risk disclaimer (RiskSheet, `-showRisk`, accepted risks) and no first-run check
  (FirstRun.swift, setup.firstRun, the region and language checks and their diagnosis):
  Brighter Shores' profile has neither. The profile parser reads only what it uses
  (setup.destination, setup.installer, setup.getApp); the copy is always its install.py.
- Copy, Install, Play and the device page (now "Pocket" under the device) speak of Brighter
  Shores alone: one copy, one update, one remove; no per-game rows or folders, and the
  device's other apps.json entries are not read. local.env has one GUEST_EXE and no
  TOLKARA_PROFILE.
- The saved state keeps one game folder, copy and executable hash. A state saved before
  (sources, copied and the install's executables keyed by "brighter-shores", the chosen
  profiles, the accepted risks) still loads: the old keys are read, the new ones written.
Upstream note: Brighter Pocket's own; Tolkara's management stays a general tool for many games.

